      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wolcott was platted in May 1861 when the railroad reached the area and named after founder Anson Wolcott.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolcott%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic Wolcott House, once on the National Register, hosts the July 4 Summer Festival every year since 1967.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolcott%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Since 2022, Wolcott passed an ordinance to be America’s quietest town, fining residents for sounds heard beyond their property line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolcott%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Wolcott Community Public Library, a cornerstone of local learning, serves residents with books and community programs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolcott%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Anson Wolcott’s ancestor, Oliver Wolcott, signed the Declaration of Independence, linking the town’s name to a founding father.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolcott%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Wolcott incorporated in 1873, dissolved two years later, and was reincorporated in 1889, reflecting early municipal challenges.",
